This comprehensive tutor by Vladimir Molodtsov contains everything needed for the beginner to the advanced player.  
This technique differs from the standard technique taught in schools since it contains a large number of exercises that will help you improve your sight-reading skills.
The time signature 6/8 and syncopations are studied separately and in great detail.Skills are developed logically and progressively from the very basic to the most advanced.  It has everything; it is packed full of the Exercises and Traditional Tunes that you will need to develop your mastery of the instrument. Enjoy!

Vancouver Trees is a mobile app that describes commonly cultivated deciduous and evergreen trees in the Metro Vancouver area. The app is available in a professional version (Vancouver Trees Pro), and in a no-frills basic version (Vancouver Trees Basic). Users of both apps can:

    · browse and search an extensive database of nearly 1,000 trees by common or scientific name, each one accurately described by its identification features, ecological needs and availability;
    · advanced search for trees based on a long list of identification features and landscape use criteria;
    · view essential information on each tree;
    · read detailed descriptions for each genus and species;
    · search a gallery of more than 2,500 tree images; and
    · view and search a glossary of more than 350 terms.


Users of Vancouver Trees Pro will also be able to:

    · share essential information on each tree;
    · view high-resolution and share low-resolution tree images from the gallery;
    · view over 3,500 mapped tree locations in the Metro Vancouver area;
    · create favourite plant lists, either to share or to make a personal archive for quick referencing; and
    · add notes on favourite lists to individually tagged plants.


The app is a comprehensive resource for landscape architects, students in landscape architecture, landscape professionals, gardeners, arborists, or anyone else with an interest in Vancouver’s trees. The app will help users to make informed decisions when planting and designing with trees. Proceeds from the sale of Vancouver Trees go to the UBC Botanical Garden.

The most functional math logic calculator.
This application has the functions as follows:
- creating truth tables;
- finding DNF, CNF, PDNF and PCNF;
- finding Zhegalkin polynomial (Undetermined coefficients method and Pascal's triangle method);
- making a Karnaugh map;
- minimizing Boolean function with equivalence conversion (both briefly and in details);
- belonging to the Post classes;
- plotting logical schemes (both IEC and ANSI schemes);
- plotting ladder diagram;
- minimizing functions using McCluskey method.
Boolean functions may be displayed as multiple characters.
Unary operation "negation" may be displayed either as a single character or in the form of an overline.

Maximum number of variables in the function is limited by 6.
Maximum number of function-embedded negations is limited by 5.
Maximum number of characters in the function is limited by 64.
Karnaugh maps, PCNF and PDNF functions, Zhegalkin polynomial and the McCluskey method only may be used for operating a value vector.
The modulus of vector shall contain 4, 8, 16, 32, or 64 characters.
The values of 0 and 1 may be used in this function but it will be subject to simplification only.
The implication is inadmissible for plotting a logical scheme.

